hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-60 = cons "**Information versus presentation cost, and exact compression.** Part I §4.4 (`lib/sort.cub`) separates three quantities on one construction (`msort`, `Fs-prop`): what list sorting forgets (the fiber of n! enumerations, or n!/∏ m_j! with multiplicities), the information resolved (log₂(n!), proved invariant across every binary sum tree by `stree-interleavings-fact`), and the work charged by a chosen presentation (C(t) = Σ depth_t(a), proved tree-dependent by `stree-cost-depths`). Knowledge compression follows the same discipline: storing each construction once by content key, factoring proofs once over general structures, and indexing every repeated sequence exactly (`lib/suffix-index.cub`, `si-index-ok`) eliminate redundancy without discarding a single distinction or path." (cons "" nil)
